.83,"ps_ratio":14.3,"fcf_to_ev":4.75,"fcf_to_mcap":1.75,"liab_to_assets":24.5,"cash_to_assets":3.9,"current_ratio":3.93,"roe":34.2,"roa":25.8,"moat":{"m1_brand_pricing":{"score":7},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":1},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":8},"m4_network_effects":{"score":3},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":9},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":2},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":8},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":8},"m10_durability":{"score":7},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Fastenal 展現了強勁的經濟護城河，主要體現在其卓越的規模成本優勢（M5）和高客戶轉換成本（M3）上。公司透過龐大的採購量和優化的供應鏈網絡，建立了難以被小型競爭者超越的成本結構。同時，其提供的 VMI 等增值服務深度綁定了客戶，顯著提高了轉換壁壘。雖然品牌（M1）和網絡效應（M4）相對較弱，但其高客戶保留率（M9）和出色的運營效率（M7）進一步鞏固了其市場地位。Fastenal 的商業模式更接近於一個高效的『收費橋』，連接供應商與龐大的工業客戶群，透過規模和服務收取費用，並在其中獲取利潤。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Fastenal possesses a strong economic moat, primarily driven by its exceptional cost advantage through scale (M5) and high customer switching costs (M3). The company has established a cost structure that is difficult for smaller competitors to match, leveraging massive purchasing volumes and an optimized supply chain network. Furthermore, value-added services like VMI deeply entrench customers, significantly raising barriers to switching. While brand (M1) and network effects (M4) are relatively weaker, its high customer retention (M9) and outstanding operational efficiency (M7) further solidify its market position. Fastenal's business model functions akin to an efficient 'toll bridge,' connecting suppliers with a vast industrial customer base, charging for access and services through scale and efficiency, thereby generating profits."},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":8,"checkedAt":null}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/FAST.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/FAST.png","website":"https://www.fastenal.com","ceo":"Jeffery Michael Watts","full_time_employees"